Market Challenges
High Treatment Costs and Unequal Access
Advanced MS therapies can involve substantial treatment expenses, creating affordability challenges for patients and healthcare systems. The report cites annual treatment costs of approximately USD 65,000–100,000 for certain targeted therapies. Actual costs vary by medicine, country, insurance coverage, and treatment arrangements.

Limited reimbursement and inadequate insurance coverage can restrict access, particularly in lower-income markets. Manufacturers, payers, and healthcare providers must balance treatment availability with financial sustainability.

Treatment Adherence and Safety Monitoring
Long-term MS management requires consistent treatment and appropriate clinical follow-up. Some therapies require regular monitoring because of potential adverse effects, infection risks, or other treatment-specific safety considerations.

Complex dosing schedules, concerns about adverse effects, and the burden of ongoing appointments may affect adherence. Clear patient education, coordinated specialist care, and appropriate monitoring can help support treatment continuity.

