Market Restraints
Stringent Regulatory and Clinical Requirements
Developing a new MS therapy requires extensive clinical research to establish safety, efficacy, and an appropriate benefit-risk profile. Pharmaceutical companies must also meet regulatory requirements for manufacturing quality, labeling, and post-marketing safety surveillance.

Long development timelines and substantial research costs can delay commercialization and increase investment risk. Continued monitoring after approval can add further operational requirements.

Treatment Complexity Across Disease Subtypes
Multiple sclerosis includes different disease courses, and treatment responses can vary between individuals. Therapies effective for one patient group may not be appropriate for another, making clinical assessment and treatment selection complex.

This variability increases the need for evidence across patient populations and can limit the applicability of individual treatment options to all forms of MS.

